###############################################################################
# 7. TEMPORAL CONTINUITY PROPERTIES  [3.3.1 - additive]
#
# Projection dependency. The behavioural stratum's TemporalQualifier dimension
# (FBO dimension 14: Standard, RetroDateApplies, ERPActive, SunsetApplies, TailCoverage,
# RunOff, MilestoneGated) had no structural source. Without a retroactive date and a
# continuity date on the claims basis, a claims-made tower projects into FBO as though it
# were unqualified, and prior-acts exclusions vanish silently.
###############################################################################

ctr:retroactiveDate
  a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain ctr:ClaimsBasisFacet ;
  rdfs:range xsd:date ;
  rdfs:label "retroactive date"@en ;
  rdfs:comment """The date before which acts, errors, omissions or occurrences are not covered,
regardless of when the resulting claim is made.

Projection: presence of this property yields FBO dimension 14 = RetroDateApplies, and the date
itself parameterises the temporal gate."""@en ;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.nebularis.org/neuro-semantic/insurance/contract> .

ctr:continuityDate
  a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain ctr:ClaimsBasisFacet ;
  rdfs:range xsd:date ;
  rdfs:label "continuity date"@en ;
  rdfs:comment """The date from which continuous cover has been maintained across successive
policy periods, used to preserve claims-made continuity on renewal and to determine whether
prior-knowledge exclusions bite.

Projection: parameterises the FBO temporal gate for ERPActive, TailCoverage and RunOff."""@en ;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.nebularis.org/neuro-semantic/insurance/contract> .

###############################################################################
# 8. CURRENCY AS A CONCEPT  [3.3.2 - additive]
#
# ctr:currency is an xsd:string. That is correct for interchange and wrong for reasoning.
# A literal cannot carry a broader relation, cannot be crosswalked, and cannot be the object
# of the FBO CurrencyFX dimension, which requires a skos:Concept. The projection functor was
# therefore binding a string into a concept-valued property and producing towers that failed
# validation on every monetary extent.
#
# The resolution keeps both. ctr:currency remains the mandatory lexical form; ctr:currencyConcept
# is the resolved node. The two are joined on skos:notation, never on the local name of the
# concept IRI, because local names are a naming convention and notations are a controlled key.
#
# The scheme is voc:CurrencyScheme in nsd-skos, not a CSO-local vocabulary. Currency is not a
# contract-structural term: the tower, exposure and claims strata all need the same concepts,
# and a fourth private copy is how the Territory and Valuation Basis duplications happened.
###############################################################################

ctr:currencyConcept
  a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:label "currency concept"@en ;
  rdfs:domain ctr:MonetaryExtent ;
  rdfs:range skos:Concept ;
  rdfs:comment """The denomination of this monetary extent as a resolved SKOS concept from
voc:CurrencyScheme.

Cardinality 0..1. Optional at capture time and expected to be materialised by resolution from
ctr:currency. Where both are present they must agree: the concept's skos:notation must equal the
string. ctr:ExtentCurrencyAgreementShape enforces that.

Consumers that aggregate across a tower must gate on this property rather than on ctr:currency.
Summing extents that differ in denomination produces a number with no referent, and the failure
is silent because the arithmetic succeeds."""@en ;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://www.nebularis.org/neuro-semantic/insurance/contract> .
